  "configuration_id": "config_046",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (multimodal, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, concat) is the best result so far at 0.532 acc, only marginally above RNA-only scvi (0.520). The image modality contributes a small but consistent boost, and we have only tested one fusion strategy (concat). Uncertainty: it is unknown whether a learned weighted fusion would better balance the dominant RNA signal against the weak image signal (image-only is only 0.227), or whether simple concatenation is already near-optimal. This experiment (config_046) changes only the fusion from concat to weighted while holding RNA encoder (scvi_n200), image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), and profile setting (singleprofile) fixed, giving a clean A/B comparison against config_005. It is the best next step because the fusion strategy is a foundational architectural choice that will condition all subsequent multimodal experiments; resolving it early prevents wasting budget on multiprofile/aggregation variants built on a suboptimal fusion, and the single-variable design maximizes interpretability under the limited budget."
}

